From: godotjs
Subject: [godotjs] node_js2c: give the iOS build the frameworks its objects need

node_js2c runs on the build machine, and on macOS its link needs CoreFoundation and
Security - the condition said OS=="mac", while an iOS build reports the destination
OS everywhere, so the frameworks were dropped and the tool's link came up short.
Same reason as the abseil patch: an Apple host link needs Apple frameworks no matter
which Apple product is being built.
diff --git a/node.gyp b/node.gyp
index 7ae1d3a..fa1bc41 100644
--- a/node.gyp
+++ b/node.gyp
@@ -1673,7 +1673,12 @@
         'src/builtin_info.cc',
       ],
       'conditions': [
-        [ 'OS=="mac"', {
+        [ 'OS in "mac ios"', {
+          # This tool runs on the build machine and links objects that call into
+          # CoreFoundation and Security (V8's code-signing cache and time-zone lookup,
+          # among them) whichever product is being produced. The destination OS for an
+          # iOS build is ios, so an ios-only or mac-only spelling left the link short
+          # of both frameworks.
           'libraries': [ '-framework CoreFoundation -framework Security' ],
         }],
         [ 'node_shared_simdutf=="false" and node_use_bundled_v8!="false"', {
